Whisper: the about:crashes page files are packaged as in Firefox

What: toolkit/crashreporter/jar.mn packages chrome://global/content/crashes.html,
crashes.js and crashes.css whether or not the crash reporter is built.
Why: Whisper builds without the crash reporter, which left these three files out.
chrome://global/ is content accessible, so a web page that tries to load them could
tell Whisper from Firefox, which has them. They are inert without the crash reporter.
gecko/scripts/webexposed.py compares every file web pages can load with Firefox's.
---
--- a/toolkit/crashreporter/jar.mn
+++ b/toolkit/crashreporter/jar.mn
@@ -3,8 +3,9 @@
 # file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
 
 toolkit.jar:
-#ifdef MOZ_CRASHREPORTER
+# Whisper: packaged without the crash reporter too, as in Firefox: web pages can load
+# these (chrome://global/ is content accessible), so their absence would identify
+# Whisper (patches/0032-crashes-page-files.patch).
   content/global/crashes.html            (content/crashes.html)
   content/global/crashes.js               (content/crashes.js)
   content/global/crashes.css              (content/crashes.css)
-#endif
